  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1200 PM CDT Sun Oct 25 2026\n\nHigh pressure maintains solid hold on our weather for nearly the\nentirety of this week. The model signals we've been discussing \nour past few AFDs for rain chances next weekend are increasing,\nbut the devil is in the details, specifically wrt to timing. \nSome deterministic modelling suggests a dry first half weekend \nwith best incoming rain chances holding off until Saturday \nnight-Sunday. The Blend picks up on that but may be overly \nbroad-brushing with its precursor rain chance Saturday. We'll \nsee how it plays out in time but that's something that offers a \nwindow of opportunity for fine-tuning given the outdoor events \nplanned around the area next weekend.\n\nTemperatures will be seasonally near perfect with upper 70s for\nhighs save a few 80F readings that pop up Wed-Fri. Lows in the\nupper 40s/around 50F push toward 60F next weekend as dews rise\nwith rain chances appearing; this heralds a continued A/A \noutlook in our 6-10 and 8-14 Temp/Pcpn projections.",
